<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">International Commission of Control</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a>–<a href="/years/1914">1914</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The International Commission of Control was a body set up by the Great Powers in 1913 to administer newly independent Albania. Made up of representatives of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, with one Albanian member, it took over from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-qemali">Ismail Qemali</a>'s provisional government and drafted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/regulamentul-organic">Organic Statute</a> of 1914. It handed power to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-prince-of-albania">Prince Wilhelm of Wied</a>, whose rule collapsed after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> began.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/international-commission-of-control.jpg" alt="International Commission of Control" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kel Marubi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:An%C3%ABtar%C3%AB_t%C3%AB_Komisionit_Nd%C3%ABrkomb%C3%ABtar_t%C3%AB_Kufinjve.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
